A||||3||d825077||lights around heater/AC||||5||
Z||000000||d825077||04-25-2000||08:49 PM||||Does anyone know how to fix the light on the heater?  When my lights are on the heater/AC does not light up.  I can not tell what is on, the vent, heater, defroster, AC or the off button.  Thank you||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodrv6||04-25-2000||09:38 PM||||You'll need to remove the trim plate that surrounds the heater control.  4 torx head bolts. Then remove the 4 hex head bolts securing the heater control head to the console support and pull the control out of the dash until you can reach the light bulb socket.  It's on the right side of the heater control.  Just twist it about a quarter turn, pull it out and replace the bulb.  I don't remember the bulb number, but the auto parts store should have a listing for it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||d825077||04-27-2000||06:18 PM||||if I put a new radio in and did not conect the dimmer wire, would that effect the lights?  If so where should I connect the dimmer wire.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jeff's '86 1/2 GT||04-27-2000||10:18 PM||||The bulb number is: 37.  It is an easy job. I just did it last night to mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||3
